			<div class="content" id="post-content-3789834">
									

<p>This will be long, but is intended just to be thorough.</p>
<p>1- Not a fault of this particular piece, actually, but I find it a little tiring how much MTFs are used. They are, to my eyes, intended as teams whose main asset is mobility. Using them as standard military, as standard special forces, or standard anything, or as more prepared/trained/awesome is something I dislike. I just had to begin with this, but lets move on.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>2- The first paragraph is eight lines long, when it could be three at most. This is overall a problem of the skip. A long read isn't a bad thing by itself, but too long without a purpose becomes tiring quickly, and this achieves to be tiring right at the start and keep being tiring almost all the way.</p>
<p>3- Why is an MTF mobilized to such a menial task as blocking and copying broadcasts? Why so much detail about the work of software designed to achieve what is still a menial task? Why so much detail on the methods used to copy and transport this data? And I thought it was obvious that any field operative should expect punishment for failing at their job. Actually, anyone with a job should.</p>
<p>Those details add nothing to the story being told, just divert from it. Broadcasts are supervised, anomalous instances are blocked and copied for analysis. This is pretty much straightforward, there is nothing unusual or unexpected on the details, and actually they seem mostly unnecessary, since they are kind of irrelevant or, in the case of the USB storage devices, specific for no reason.</p>
<p>4- Second paragraph is even worse. You could say just &quot;evidence should be destroyed per standard procedure, and civilian witnesses administered Class-B amnestics&quot;. Everything else just divert from your story, giving unnecessary details and even citing O-5 decision for no real purpose but to say that O-5 can overrule protocol and order atrocities if the shit hits the fan royally. Like they can do with any other SCP.</p>
<p>5- The third paragraph thoroughly states the obvious when it should just read &quot;personnel affected can be treated with Class-C amnestics&quot;. The last paragraph on containment makes nothing except state that information about the skip is effectively public internally. It both makes the previous paragraph even more irrelevant (since you will destroy evidence for a population that you provide with evidence) and this skip the most easily known in the entire Foundation.</p>
<p>6- REVISION 3-08 makes it seem that this cognitohazard is somehow more seductive than all the thousand other cognitohazard, to the point where you must tell trained personnel that you shouldn't watch the thing that makes you nuts when you watch it. O-5 themselves had to step out to tell them that this is forbidden. Sorry, but this paragraph is very stupid.</p>
<p>7- First paragraph of Description isn't so bad, actually. It could be trimmed, and the failure rate of the USDPA doesn't seem like a necessary development, but isn't bad either. What it does lack, though, is an actual description. It states that the ad is distorted and full of esoteric messages, but it doesn't really describes nothing about the ad outside there being an &quot;unnamed corporation&quot;. Show, don't tell.</p>
<p>8- The bullet-points about the effects put a lot of focus on effects that don't seem that anomalous, actually. It is cumbersome and divert from what really makes the anomaly, well, anomalous. You see, a lot of people believe in a lot of things with &quot;sudden, unexplained interest&quot;. It seems more like the descriptions of common things you see in -Js, until far later, when it states that the person effectively evolve this interest into obsession. And the compulsion to spread the anomaly is given so little attention here it isn't really clear until the end of the second Case File.</p>
<p>Put less words in this, and focus those words on what makes your anomaly unique. Make it clear that those UFO-nuts are way more nuts than others. If you want perfectly sane people to be affected, it should be obvious that some of those people shouldn't be into this stuff.</p>
<p>9- Blanking exsanguination just to state it in parenthesis isn't cool. Get out the black boxes if you don't need them. Stating that the number of known subjects is unknown isn't, either, unless the anomaly also blurs the notion of numbers.</p>
<p>10- Case File 01 not only do no good at all to the skip. Creating a useless wall of text just to describe an actual person and use his photo is, AFAIK, against the site policies. You could just add a short one line citation and link the wikipedia page about Robert Lazar:<br />
<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bob_Lazar">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bob_Lazar</a></p>
<p>11- Addendum II, the interview, is a lot better and have some potential, but is still more confusing on its purpose than actually adding a sense of confusion. Who's James Fritz? Why the interviewer is so careless? What is the context of this? It shows that the guy is in negation of what he did, but otherwise I see no reason whatsoever to care about this entire interview, I don't have enough context for this to say anything whatsoever.</p>
<p>12- Addedum III is clearly the centerpiece, and is rightly so. It isn't bad at all. But the previous text already lagged so much I'm tired when I finally reach here. Also, there are some very awkward decisions on the part of the Foundation on this event.</p>
<p>Was there a search for the missing security?</p>
<p>How did the Foundation took 24 minutes to arrive, but just 7 to investigate the scene, cover evidence and lift lock down?</p>
<p>Why did they released O'Connor before gathering more info from him?</p>
<p>What was actually examined and found about Jessica, the bathroom, her office and her body?</p>
<p>Why no one asked why Thomas fled so promptly? He is the only unharmed witness of the entities.</p>
<p>How did Carl West became a medical officer at just 13?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<em>As a courtesy to our readers on mobile devices, please collapse long posts. ~Zyn</em><br />
.<br />
.<br />
.<br />
And that's it. The last pieces on Carl West can be trimmed a bit, but are overall a good ending. They do need a better context, though, and the text failed on providing this. It still can work, though, just needs a serious rewrite.
							</div>

								
